00:54:15.401 --> 00:54:17.755
I think networking people,

00:54:17.756 --> 00:54:22.735
by training, are sort of
like to be predictable.

00:54:22.736 --> 00:54:25.760
The RFC specify
what protocols must

00:54:25.761 --> 00:54:28.875
do and if it's not a must
it's at least assured.

00:54:28.876 --> 00:54:31.270
If such a message comes
this is what you should do.

00:54:31.271 --> 00:54:32.190
If there's a packet lost

00:54:32.191 --> 00:54:33.385
this is what you
