because it's just a map.

00:55:25.231 --> 00:55:28.140
It's a signal.
That's an advantage.

00:55:28.141 --> 00:55:30.830
It doesn't need to
know the nature

00:55:30.831 --> 00:55:34.220
of the noise. It's
going to learn.

00:55:34.221 --> 00:55:37.350
So, I think it's
mostly that there's

00:55:37.351 --> 00:55:42.990
certain factors that function
as learnable that

00:55:42.991 --> 00:55:44.495
really is most of
the work goes in

00:55:44.496 --> 00:55:47.125
establishing that fact and then

00:55:47.126 --> 00:55:51.900
you trying using a neural
network to learn that function.

00:55:51.901 --> 00:55:54.940
In the case of music, it
wasn't straightforward.

00:55:54.941 --> 00:55:57.045
You really had to
work quite hard.

00:55:57.046 --> 00:56:00.180
So, often shelf stuff
doesn't work.

00:56:00.950 --> 00:56:04.000
But it wasn't much doubt
that function is

00:56:04.001 --> 00:56:06.240
learnable because we know what

00:56:06.241 --> 00:56:09.760
the function is and it's
got continuous parts

00:56:09.761 --> 00:56:14.750
and lends itself just
visually into learnable.

00:56:14.870 --> 00:56:17.730
So, I think that's one thing
about this question of

00:56:17.731 --> 00:56:20.505
whether do you want data models,

00:56:20.506 --> 00:56:22.300
the way you train these models

00:56:22.301 --> 00:56:24.895
frankly is you need data
just to begin with.

00:56:24.896 --> 00:56:27.120
Much of what we did or anybody's

00:56:27.121 --> 00:56:29.825
doing it just requires it.

00:56:29.826 --> 00:56:32.115
Whenever you're trying to
learn a function y equals

00:56:32.116 --> 00:56:34.485
f of x, in a lot of it X,

00:56:34.486 --> 00:56:39.735
I, Y pairs, then the function
has to be learnable.

00:56:39.736 --> 00:56:43.700
So, that's really what I've seen.

00:56:43.701 --> 00:56:46.060
There may be some cases
where the function

00:56:46.061 --> 00:56:47.930
has some very bad sort of

